[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   step_157: conventional generative population model for the arrival
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   anisotropy (b123).
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   Step 149 (b113) showed that Newtonian dynamics *transmits* an
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   incoming-direction anisotropy into the periapsis-rotation field, and
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   step 152 (b116) priced the conditioned nulls on the *observed* arrival
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   directions.  Neither is generative: both condition on the catalogued
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   directions.  This step closes the loop -- it GENERATES an incoming
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   population under conventional physics, passes it through a simulated
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   discovery-selection function, and asks whether the resulting synthetic
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   arrival-direction distribution reproduces the observed cap excess.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   Conventional chain
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   1. Source: isotropic Oort-spike aphelion directions u on the sphere.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   2. Galactic-tide injection: for each u, the per-orbit secular drift
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   of perihelion distance is computed by integrating the tidal torque
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   r x (T . r) over the unperturbed eccentric orbit (impulse/secular
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   approximation; the same tide tensor as step_070:  diag(+OmG^2,
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   -OmG^2, -4 pi G rho) in the Galactic frame).  The orbit's
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   angular-momentum direction h sweeps a uniform circle perpendicular
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   to u.  Two injection weights are evaluated:
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   w_flux(u)  = <max(0, -Dq)> over h orientations -- the standard
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   loss-cone filling-flux proxy (per-orbit downward
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   drift across the observability boundary);
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   w_hard(u)  = fraction of h draws with q0 + Dq < q_loss for
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   q0 = 8 AU, q_loss = 5 AU.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   3. Stellar-impulse diffusion (model M2): the injected density is
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   mixed with an isotropic component -- passing stars randomise
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   the source on ~Gyr timescales, so a fraction f_iso of the arrival
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   density is isotropic.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   4. Discovery selection: rejection sampling against the empirical
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   ecliptic-latitude detection kernel, kappa(beta) = smoothed
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   observed latitude density / uniform density -- the first-order
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   pointing model, exactly the conditioning step_152 applies but
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   used here as a generative filter.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   5. Planetary diffusion to observable q is treated as direction-
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   independent (inclination-averaged); stated as an assumption.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   Models
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   M0  isotropic source x selection            (selection-only control)
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   M1  isotropic source x tide  x selection    (canonical conventional)
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   M2  M1 + isotropic stellar remixing f_iso=0.5
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   M3  tide injection alone, no selection      (raw tidal signature)
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   Tests (per model, matched n=54 and all-class-1 n=131 samples)
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   T1  predicted in-cap fraction distribution vs the observed
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   22/54 = 40.7% and 48/131 = 36.6% (60-deg cap on the resident
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   axis).  p_model = fraction of synthetic samples with f >= f_obs.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   T2  the model density's own preferred direction (resultant of the
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   predicted sky density) and its separation from the resident
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   axis -- does conventional generation have any reason to point
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   at (49, -17)?
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   T3  per-sample resultant direction vs the axis: rank of the observed
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   sample's axis-proximity among synthetic samples.
[2026-09-21 15:42:01 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 157]   Inputs
